# Intentionally NOT a valid certificate.
#
# The JWT verification cert MUST be supplied at runtime via KMS-synced config
# (jwtPublicKeyBase64 / jwtPublicKey in app.conf) — see controllers/account.go
# InitAuthConfig. This placeholder is the embedded fallback: it is deliberately
# not a parseable PEM, so if the config cert is ever missing, signature
# verification FAILS CLOSED (rejects every token) instead of trusting a shipped
# key. The previous embedded value was an upstream default keypair whose private
# key is published — trusting it on missing config was a fail-open auth bypass.
# Do not put a real cert here.
